'''Neyo''', designated '''CC-8826''', was an [[Advanced Recon Commando]] who served in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]], rising to become a [[Clone Marshal Commander]] and the leader of the [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]]. [[Cloning|Bred]] from the [[DNA|genetic]] [[Clone template|template]] of the [[human]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]] and for the sole purpose of combat, Neyo developed a cold personality.

As the war with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] progressed, the [[Republic Military]] formed a special team of [[droid]]s known as [[D-Squad]]. Neyo's [[DUM-series pit droid]], designated [[WAC-47]], was transferred from the 91st to the new [[squad]] under [[Colonel]] [[Meebur Gascon]]'s leadership. Later, the commander attended a [[Republic strategy conference]] at the [[Valor (space station)|''Valor'']] [[space station]] located in the [[Carida system]]. During the conference, a [[Carida incident|Separatist attack]] on the station was thwarted by the members of D-Squad, including Neyo's former droid.

Neyo and his [[troop]]s were stationed on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Saleucami]], under the command of [[Jedi General]] [[Stass Allie]], in the waning [[Standard day|days]] of the Clone Wars. While patrolling the planet's surface, he received a message from the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Sidious]] instructing him to execute [[Order 66]]. As a clone [[Behavioral modification biochip|conditioned]] to obey the secret protocol, Neyo fired his [[BARC speeder]]'s [[laser cannon]]s on the [[general]], adding Allie to the list of [[Jedi]] who [[Death|perished]] in the initial [[Great Jedi Purge]] that preceded the [[Imperial Era|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].

==Biography==
===Early life===
CC-8826 was the designation of a [[clone trooper]] who went by the name of Neyo during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Databank" /> Prior to the pan-[[The galaxy|galactic]] conflict, Neyo was [[Cloning|created]] on the [[extragalactic]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Kamino]] as part of a clone [[army]] grown in secret to serve the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Clone Troopers">{{Databank|clone-troopers|Clone Troopers}}</ref> At the [[First Battle of Geonosis|start]] of the [[Clone Wars]] between the Republic and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]]<ref name="GAR">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Grand Army of the Republic}}</ref> in [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> Neyo served as an [[Advanced Recon Commando]] within the [[Grand Army of the Republic]]. Neyo then joined the experimental [[ARC program]] on Kamino, which was designed to provide the Republic with a new, elite force that was capable of confronting the expanding [[Separatist Droid Army]].<ref name="GAR" />

During training, Neyo and the other [[clone cadet]]s began to develop a personality of their own, which was a phenomenon that was fostered by the unusual methodology of the program. Its designers saw this as a positive trait, as it gave the clones greater independent thought and greater freedom of expression compared to conventional clones.<ref name="GAR" /> Despite this, Neyo developed a cold personality,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> and was considered to be one of the most aloof and oddball members of the program, failing to bond with his comrades. Another clone, [[Bacara]], was also considered brooding and the two clones eventually collaborated on the development and field trials of tactics that used the newly produced [[BARC speeder]]s. Neyo was one of the first one hundred graduates of the ARC program, and was given the [[military rank]] of [[Clone Marshal Commander]]. Shortly after his promotion, Neyo was placed as the [[commanding officer]] of the [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]].<ref name="GAR" />

===Clone Wars continues===
====Capture of Adi Gallia====
[[Commander]] Neyo's first Jedi General was [[Jedi Master]] [[Adi Gallia]], who was long-[[time]] member of the [[Jedi High Council]] and considered an excellent commander. Although Gallia's [[flagship]] was a [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]], she changed her transport on several occasions. In one such instance, [[Supreme Martial Commander of the Separatist Droid Armies]] [[General]] [[Grievous]] attacked her [[Adi Gallia's flagship|flagship]] in a surprise [[Battle of Patitite Pattuna|assault]] and forced her to abandon ship. As a result, Gallia was separated from Commander Neyo and the rest of her men long enough for Grievous to capture her. The survivors were rescued by Jedi General [[Plo Koon]] and his [[104th Battalion]], and immediately launched a rescue mission. [[Plo Koon's second fleet|Plo Koon's fleet]] attacked Grievous' flagship and [[Rescue of Adi Gallia|freed]] Gallia.<ref name="HC 33">{{HelmetCollectionCite|33|Helmets}}</ref>

====D-Squad's mission====
[[File:Neyo_in_Temple.png|thumb|left|250px|Like other clone troopers, Neyo served under the Jedi Order during the Clone Wars.]]
During the war, Neyo possessed a [[DUM-series pit droid]], designated [[WAC-47]], that reported to him while serving with the [[corps]].<ref name="WAC-47">{{Databank|wac-47|WAC-47}}</ref> By [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> [[Commander]] Neyo escorted WAC-47 to the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] for a briefing on a new mission. WAC-47's bad hearing made them arrive late and interrupt [[Jedi General]] [[Mace Windu]]'s briefing to [[R2-D2]], [[M5-BZ]], [[QT-KT]], [[U9-C4]], and their owners. After mission leader [[Colonel]] [[Meebur Gascon]] arrived, Windu, Neyo, and the others left the briefing for Gascon's [[D-Squad]].<ref name="Secret Weapons">{{TCW|Secret Weapons}}</ref>

Neyo later attended a [[Republic strategy conference|strategy conference]] aboard the [[Valor (space station)|''Valor'']] [[space station]] in the [[Carida system]] alongside other clone officers such as [[Clone Marshal Commander]] [[Cody]] and Clone Commander [[Wolffe]], [[Republic officer]]s including [[Admiral]]s [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], [[Barton Coburn]], and [[Wullf Yularen]], as well as Jedi officers consisting of Windu, [[High Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], and Jedi General [[Anakin Skywalker]].<ref name="Point of No Return">{{TCW|Point of No Return (The Clone Wars)}}</ref> The members were there to analyze the open war against the Separatists.<ref name="GAR" /> With the [[Republic Military]]'s high-[[Military rank|ranking]] officials gathered in a single location, the Separatists conspired to wipe them out using a commandeered [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]], the ''[[Renown]]'' outfitted with [[rhydonium]]. However, the station&mdash;along with Neyo and its other occupants&mdash;was ultimately saved from destruction due to the [[Carida incident|intervention]] of D-Squad.<ref name="Point of No Return" />

Later, Neyo sent out the survival compendium "[[Neyo's Almanac of Clankers]]" to the [[Clone Youth Brigade]] that described battle droids used by the Separatists.<ref name="Official Magazine 118">{{GermanFanCite|118|Database}}</ref>

===Outer Rim Sieges===
{{Quote|Execute Order 66.|Darth Sidious's command to the clone troopers|audio=ExecuteOrder66.flac|<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref>}}
[[File:StassAllieDeath.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Neyo carried out Order 66 by executing his Jedi general, Stass Allie, while serving with her on Saleucami.]]
In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> Commander Neyo has participated in many battles in the [[Outer Rim Sieges]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Eventually he and his 91st were placed under the command of Jedi General [[Oppo Rancisis]] to retake the [[planet]] [[Saleucami]], which was held by the Separatists.<ref name="GAR" /> During this time, Neyo sent out an expansion to his Almanac of Clankers, with the help of WAC-47.<ref name="OSWM 121">{{GermanFanCite|121|Database}}</ref> The [[Siege of Saleucami]] was a long and complicated campaign, but the world was ultimately taken by Republic forces. After the defeat of the Separatists, Commander Neyo and the rest of the 91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps remained on Saleucami while the rest of the Republic troops departed. Neyo and his forces remained under the command of Jedi General [[Stass Allie]], who was placed in charge of patrolling the planet for any Separatist strongholds<ref name="GAR" /> and remove the remaining pockets of resistance.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

During one patrol, Commander Neyo and one of his [[Unidentified clone lieutenant|clone lieutenants]] accompanied General Allie on BARC speeders on a patrol through a battlefield on Saleucami when the two clones received [[Order 66]]<ref name="Episode III" /> directly<ref name="HC 33" /> from the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Sidious]], who was publicly the [[Supreme Chancellor]] of the Republic Sheev Palpatine.<ref name="Episode III" /> The directive activated the [[behavioral modification biochip]]s which compelled the clones to follow the order and [[Death|kill]] any [[Jedi]].<ref name="Conspiracy">{{TCW|Conspiracy}}</ref> As a result, Commander Neyo and his wingman fell back behind their Jedi General and fired on her speeder, destroying it<ref name="Episode III" /> and killing Stass Allie instantly.<ref name="GAR" /> The implementation of Order 66 commenced the [[Great Jedi Purge]], and the Republic was subsequently [[Proclamation of the New Order|reorganized]] into the [[Galactic Empire]] with Sidious anointing himself as [[Galactic Emperor]].<ref name="Episode III" /> Commander Neyo returned to the area of concentration of Republic troops to leave the planet, and subsequently continued to serve in the new Galactic Empire within the [[Imperial Army]].<ref name="GAR" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Neyo.png|thumb|right|200px|Neyo in his Phase II armor]]
Commander Neyo was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] clone<ref name="Databank" /> of [[Jango Fett]], a [[bounty hunter]] and the [[DNA|genetic]] [[Clone template|template]] of the [[Kaminoan]] clone army.<ref name="Clone Troopers" /> As such, he inherited the physical traits of his progenitor, including a height of 1.83 [[meter]]s,<ref name="Databank" /> [[Color|black]] [[hair]], brown [[eye]]s, and tan skin. During the Clone Wars, he had a facial [[tattoo]] printed in [[Aurebesh]] [[writing]], which read "CC-8826."<ref name="Episode Guide" /> As with the rest of the clone army,<ref name="Fugitive">{{TCW|Fugitive}}</ref> Neyo was programmed to execute Order 66 upon its authorization by Darth Sidious.<ref name="Episode III" /> Being bred solely for combat, Neyo developed a disturbingly cold personality.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==Skills and abilities==
Neyo was trained in the ARC program, and as a clone officer was skilled in armed and unarmed combat, military tactics, reconnaissance, and speeder [[pilot]]ing.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> He was also skilled in leadership and obedience, with him and his forces also being experts in quietly gathering intelligence in the field on enemy deployments, defenses, and firepower. Neyo was considered one of the most experienced commanders in the Republic Army, and although he was extremely loyal, he could not disobey Order 66.<ref name="HC 33" />

==Equipment==
Commander Neyo utilized the modified variant of standard [[Phase II clone trooper armor]] worn by [[Biker Advanced Recon Commando]]s (BARC troopers) with a command belt indicating his status as an ARC trooper. Additionally, his [[armor]] was decorated with four emblems of the 91st, on his [[helmet]], on the chest, and the other two on his right bicep and thigh respectively.<ref name="GAR" /> He was in possession of a BARC speeder at the time of Order 66,<ref name="Databank" /> and therefore used its [[laser cannon]]s to fire on [[General]] Stass Allie.<ref name="Episode III" />

==Behind the scenes==
CC-8826 "Neyo" first appeared in the film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']]. Like all clone troopers in the [[prequel trilogy]], Neyo was portrayed through computer-generated imagery.<ref name="Episode III" /> According to [[Pablo Hidalgo]], the basis of Neyo's CT-number came from his parents' landline phone number.<ref name="Pablo Tweet on Neyo">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1393811656908492806|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=Yes. And it became the basis of Clone Commander Neyo's number.|archivefile=File:Neyo-Number-Origin.png}}</ref>

